---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import BusinessPerspectiveNote from '../../components/BusinessPerspectiveNote.astro';
import ToolNextStep from '../../components/ToolNextStep.astro';
import StudyAbroadReadinessPlanner from '../../components/StudyAbroadReadinessPlanner.astro';

const title = 'Study Abroad Readiness Planner: Cost, Visa and Backup';
const description = 'Check the full cost, official sources, visa rules and backup plan before you pay a study-abroad deposit. Dated steps and questions to send. Free.';
const canonical = 'https://futurecareerschool.com/tools/study-abroad-readiness-planner/';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <Nav activePage="tools" />
  <BusinessPerspectiveNote />
  <main>
    <section class="tool-hero container"><p class="eyebrow">FREE STUDY-ABROAD PLANNER</p><h1>Study Abroad Readiness <span>Planner</span></h1><p class="lead">Look at the whole decision, not only the university offer or the country's marketing. Enter the cost and what you have checked to get dated steps, the money gap and questions to send in writing.</p><p class="tool-limits">Apply on the university website. No agent can promise admission or a visa. Use current official sources for visa, work and cost rules.</p></section>
    <section class="container tool-shell"><StudyAbroadReadinessPlanner /></section>
    <section class="container tool-explainer"><h2>Make an international study decision reviewable</h2><div class="explainer-grid"><article><h3>Check the route</h3><p>Keep the university's claims apart from the government rules on visas, work and recognition.</p></article><article><h3>Map the full cost</h3><p>Add deposits, living, travel, insurance, currency movement and a cushion, not only tuition.</p></article><article><h3>Keep a backup</h3><p>A return, lower-cost or staged route protects the family if funding or work plans change.</p></article></div>
    <h2>A worked example (an illustration, not real fees)</h2><p>A family looks at a 2-year master's course. Tuition is ₹25,00,000 a year, living is ₹10,00,000 a year and one-time costs are ₹4,00,000, so the total is ₹74,00,000 or ₹37,00,000 a year.</p><p>The family can give ₹15,00,000, so ₹59,00,000 is missing. That is the number to test with a loan EMI at a salary they are sure of, before any deposit is paid.</p>
    <h2>When to talk to a person</h2><p>Before you pay, ask the university's international office the written questions in the result. Ask your bank about loans and the rules for sending money abroad, and talk to a counsellor who does not earn a commission from the university.</p></section>
    <ToolNextStep toolName="Study Abroad Readiness Planner" audience="graduate" />
  </main><Footer />
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .tool-hero{padding:5rem 1.25rem 2rem}.tool-hero h1{max-width:850px}.tool-hero h1 span{color:var(--gold,#e5b84a)}.lead{max-width:760px;font-size:1.15rem;line-height:1.7}.tool-limits{max-width:760px;font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted,#b9c2c1)}.tool-shell{max-width:1050px}.tool-explainer{padding:2rem 1.25rem 5rem}.tool-explainer h2{margin-top:0}.explainer-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:1rem}.explainer-grid article{padding:1rem;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14);border-radius:14px}.explainer-grid h3{margin-top:0}@media(max-width:720px){.tool-hero{padding-top:3rem}.explainer-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
